Today I learned about creating files in linux

In linux there are many ways to create file like using commandlines like cat, touch, echo and nano or create directly from File System

The way I use to create file is that I use command lines to do so

Here are the command lines and there details

1. cat
= 'cat" is a command line used to read files
Syntax:
cat file_name

2. touch
= "touch" is a command line used to create empty files
Syntax:
touch file_name

multiple files at dedicated location
syntax:
touch destination/{file1,file2}

3. echo
= "echo" is a command line used to print single line files
Syntax:
echo "Text" > file_name  =  This is to write a line in the file, if somethings are already written then it removes the existing one with the one
that's just written

echo "Text" >> file_name   =  This is to append/overwrite the written things in the file

4. nano 
=  "nano" is the best commandline for file writing and editing because nano is a whole file editor in itself, easy to use plus easy to manage files.
Syntax:
nano file_name  =  After this the whole file editior will open after this you can write/edit your file easily.


This is how you can create a file in linux
